          "text": "S1: Definitions and assumptions.\n\n### Stipulated abstract model\n\nLet `Transition` be an arbitrary type of candidate transitions. Let\n\n- `GBP : Transition \u2192 Prop`,\n- `BD : Transition \u2192 Prop`,\n- `OC : Transition \u2192 Prop`\n\nbe predicates on candidate transitions.\n\nDefine abstract admissibility by\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{ALLOW}(t) \\;:\\!\\iff\\; GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t).\n\\]\n\nNo further properties of `Transition`, `GBP`, `BD`, or `OC` are assumed.\n\n### Lean 4 definition candidate\n\n```lean\nuniverse u\n\nvariable {Transition : Type u}\n\nvariable (GBP BD OC : Transition \u2192 Prop)\n\ndef ALLOW (t : Transition) : Prop :=\n  GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t\n```\n\nThis is an unverified logical-core candidate, not evidence about any concrete implementation.\n\n### Generated claim target\n\nFor every `t : Transition`, the intended necessary-and-sufficient characterization is\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{ALLOW}(t)\\iff GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t).\n\\]\n\nIts two directions are:\n\n- Necessity: `ALLOW t \u2192 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t`.\n- Sufficiency: `GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t \u2192 ALLOW t`.\n\nNo proof or Lean verification is asserted at this stage.\n\n### Claim boundary\n\nThe definitions concern only the stipulated abstract evaluator. They do not establish that any deployed or concrete GCAT/BCAT implementation computes these predicates correctly, applies this decision rule, or conforms to the characterization.\n\n### Unresolved implementation evidence\n\nNo concrete evaluator source, predicate binding, execution evidence, or implementation-conformance proof has been provided."
